## Examples

### Good Example
```go
// Implementation following guidelines
```

### Bad Example
```go
// Implementation not following guidelines
```

## AI Assistant Checklist

- [ ] Checklist item 1
- [ ] Checklist item 2
```

### Bad Rule Structure
```markdown
# Rule Title

Some content without clear structure.

More content scattered throughout.

No clear sections or examples.
```

## Cross-Reference Guidelines

### 1. Related Rules Section
Include a section that references related rules:

```markdown
## Related Rules

This rule works in conjunction with:
- **Rule Name**: Brief description of relationship
- **Another Rule**: Brief description of relationship
```

### 2. See Also References
Use inline references to other rules:

```markdown
For more details, see [Rule Name](mdc:rule-name).
```

## Practical Examples Guidelines

### 1. Code Examples
- Include complete, working code examples
- Show both good and bad implementations
- Use realistic scenarios from the spooky codebase
- Include error handling examples

### 2. Real-World Scenarios
- Describe common use cases
- Include troubleshooting guidance
- Show integration patterns
- Provide migration examples

### 3. Anti-Patterns
- Clearly identify what not to do
- Explain why patterns are problematic
- Provide alternatives
- Include consequences of violations

